///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Author: Sebastian Lindner
//
// Description: Explicit divisor ADDITION in WEIGHTED PROJECTIVE coordinates for
//              the genus-3 ramified model, characteristic neither 2 nor 7:
//
//              f(x) = x^7 + f5x^5 + f4x^4 + f3x^3 + f2x^2 + f1x + f0
//
//              Companion to nch2_ramifiedG3_DBL.mag in this directory. Same
//              grading, same single auxiliary coordinate, no field inversion.
//
// Why an addition at all, when a VDF's delay is pure squaring: the VERIFIER is
//              general exponentiation, roughly 2*lambda doublings and lambda/2
//              additions independent of T, and it is the half that has to be fast.
//              Eval is the half that is supposed to be slow. So the addition is
//              co-primary, not secondary.
//
// TWO ENTRY POINTS, and the distinction is the input convention, not the maths:
//
//   Deg3ADD     both divisors projective on INDEPENDENT Z1, Z2. Unconditionally
//               applicable, and the shape Fan-Wollinger-Gong publish, so it is the
//               apples-to-apples comparison: 87M + 13S = 100 against their
//               123M + 7S = 130. Measured 86M 13S 61A 1C 0I.
//
//   Deg3ADDmix  one operand projective, one AFFINE. The verifier's inner loop -- a
//               windowed exponentiation adds a precomputed, normalised table entry
//               to a projective accumulator -- and about 38% of its operation
//               budget. Measured 75M 10S 61A 1C 0I, against FWG's mixed 104M + 6S.
//               The precondition is cheap because the table is built up front, so
//               Montgomery's batch trick applies there and NOT in the delay chain.
//
//              A shared-Z variant exists and measures 66M 9S 61A 1C, and is
//              deliberately NOT shipped: two operands share a denominator only if
//              both came out of one computation and neither was renormalised, which
//              a double-and-add ladder does not produce. It is the prettiest number
//              here and the least realisable.
//
// Grading:     as the doubling. wt(x) = 2, wt(y) = 2g+1 = 7, so
//                  u_i = U_i/Z^(2(e-i))   for a monic u of degree e
//                  v_j = V_j/Z^(7-2j)     on every branch, e-independent
//              The u exponents shift with the output degree and the v exponents do
//              not, which is what lets these files keep the shipped bottom-aligned
//              return shape rather than inverting the affine convention.
//
// Curve coefficients arrive RAW. These functions carry them themselves -- see the
//              Z ladder at the top of each -- so a caller that pre-scales applies
//              the carriage twice: correct at Z = 1 and wrong at every other Z.
//
// PARAMETER NAMES ARE THE DERIVATION'S, NOT HOUSE STYLE, and that is a knowing
//              deviation recorded rather than hidden. Renaming to u/v/up/vp is
//              blocked: every target name ALREADY OCCURS in both bodies as an
//              internal value, so a whole-token rename would merge an input with an
//              unrelated intermediate -- PR21's exact hazard, where u1_1 -> u1
//              silently merged with a polynomial u1. PR21 was an entire PR for that
//              work on the affine files, 7,310 replacements with a drift guard, and
//              doing it inline here is how a silent wrong answer ships. The rename
//              is follow-up work and must be TWO-PHASE: move the internal names
//              first, then the parameters.
//
//              So the mapping is documented instead, and it was established by
//              MEASUREMENT against reference.add rather than read off the names --
//              the alternative assignment disagrees. Note in particular that the
//              orders are not uniform: three different ones appear below.
//
// Scope:       FREQUENT PATH ONLY, as the doubling. The degenerate addition
//              branches -- ADD24, ADD26, ADD28 through ADD33, ADD35 in both arb and
//              nch2 -- are NOT quasi-homogeneous statement by statement: each
//              contains a Karatsuba cross-term fold (a+b)*(c+d) - a*c - b*d where a
//              and b are adjacent coefficients of one polynomial, and adjacent
//              coefficients differ by exactly 2 in weight. The fold is exact, so the
//              VALUE is graded and the STATEMENT is not. Fixing it is 23
//              re-associations at +15M -69A whole-file and nothing on the frequent
//              path; until then ADD refuses what it does not implement.
//
///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

//Must keep next line in this format for latex conversion
//Constant: f5,f4,f3,f2,f1,f0

//Coordinates: projective
//Weights: u2=2,u1=4,u0=6,v2=3,v1=5,v0=7,up2=2,up1=4,up0=6,vp2=3,vp1=5,vp0=7,f5=4,f4=6,f3=8

///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Deg3ADDmix():
// Input: Z:                  the PROJECTIVE operand's denominator, nonzero
//        f5:                 curve coefficient, RAW
//        ap2,ap1,ap0:        AFFINE operand's u coefficients, DESCENDING
//        bp2,bp1,bp0:        AFFINE operand's v coefficients, DESCENDING
//        u0,u1,u2:           PROJECTIVE operand's u numerators -- ASCENDING, and
//                            that is not a typo. This signature carries three
//                            different coefficient orders; see the file banner.
//        v2,v1,v0:           PROJECTIVE operand's v numerators, DESCENDING
//
// Output: upp3, upp2, upp1, upp0, vpp2, vpp1, vpp0, Znew, as Deg3ADD.
//
// Description: Adds a projective divisor to an AFFINE one. Measured
//              75M 10S 61A 1C 0I, eleven multiplicative operations under the general
//              case, because only six coordinates need lifting instead of twelve and
//              no denominator unification is needed.
//
//              THE PRIMED NAMES ARE THE AFFINE OPERAND. Verified against
//              reference.add: the transposed assignment disagrees. Addition is
//              commutative, so a swapped call can still return a correct answer for
//              a symmetric input -- which is exactly why this is stated rather than
//              left to the reader, and why a test using two Z = 1 operands would
//              pass either mapping.
///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
Deg3ADDmix:= function(Z, f5, ap2, ap1, ap0, bp2, bp1, bp0, u0, u1, u2, v2, v1, v0)
    Z2 := Z^2;
    Z4 := Z2^2;
    F5 := f5*Z4;
    Z3 := Z2*Z;
    Z5 := Z4*Z;
    Z6 := Z3^2;
    Z7 := Z6*Z;
    up2 := ap2*Z2;
    up1 := ap1*Z4;
    up0 := ap0*Z6;
    vp2 := bp2*Z3;
    vp1 := bp1*Z5;
    vp0 := bp0*Z7;
    t1 := u0 - up0;
    t4 := u1 - up1;
    t7 := u2 - up2;
    t2 := -up0*t7;
    t5 := t1 - up1*t7;
    t8 := t4 - up2*t7;
    m7 := t4*t8 - t5*t7;
    m8 := t2*t7 - t1*t8;
    m9 := t1*t5 - t2*t4;
    m5 := m9 + up2*m8;
    m2 := -up0*m7;
    m1 := m5 + up1*m7;
    d := t1*m1 + t4*m2 + t2*m8;
    k2 := F5 - u1 + u2^2;
    vt2 := vp2 - v2;
    vt1 := vp1 - v1;
    vt0 := vp0 - v0;
    m3 := -up0*m8;
    sp0 := vt0*m1 + vt1*m2 + vt2*m3;
    sp1 := vt0*(m8 + up2*m7) + vt1*m5 + vt2*(m2 - up1*m8);
    sp2 := vt0*m7 + vt1*m8 + vt2*m9;
    A2 := sp2^2;
    G := up2*sp2 - sp1;
    R1 := up1*A2 - sp1*G - sp0*sp2;
    R0 := up0*A2 - sp0*G;
    P := sp2*d;
    P2 := P^2;
    P3 := P2*P;
    P4 := P2^2;
    P5 := P4*P;
    P6 := P3^2;
    P7 := P6*P;
    W := P*d;
    Ls1 := sp1*W;
    Lw3 := W^2;
    Lr1 := R1;
    Lr0 := R0*P2;
    Lu2 := u2*P2;
    Lup2 := up2*P2;
    Lv2 := v2*P3;
    Lvt2 := vt2*P3;
    Lkmu := (k2 - up1)*P4;
    Lu1 := u1*P4;
    Lv1 := v1*P5;
    Lu0 := u0*P6;
    Lv0 := v0*P7;
    Lt7 := Lu2 - Lup2;
    Lv2p := Lv2 + Lv2 + Lvt2;
    Lq0 := Lup2 - Ls1;
    LM10 := Lvt2 + Lr0 + Lr1*Lt7;
    LM21 := -Lu2 - Ls1;
    LM20 := Lkmu + Ls1*(Lu2 + Lup2) + Lr1*Lv2p;
    LE := LM21 - Lr1^2;
    Lupp2 := LE + Lq0;
    Lupp1 := LM20 - Lr1*(LM10 + Lr0) + LM21*Lq0;
    Lupp0 := LM20*Lq0 - Lr0*LM10;
    Lt1 := Lr0 - Lr1*Lq0;
    Lt2 := (Lu2 - Lq0)*Lt1 + LE*Lw3;
    Lvpp2 := Lr1*(Lu2 - Lupp2) + Lt1 + Lw3 - Lv2;
    Lvpp1 := Lr1*(Lu1 - Lupp1) + Lt2 - Lv1;
    Lvpp0 := Lr1*(Lu0 - Lupp0) + Lu1*Lt1 - Lq0*Lt2 + Lupp1*Lw3 - Lv0;
    Znew := P*Z;
    return 1, Lupp2, Lupp1, Lupp0, Lvpp2, Lvpp1, Lvpp0, Znew;
end function;


///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Deg3ADD():
// Input: Z1, Z2:            the two operands' independent denominators, both nonzero
//        X2,X1,X0, Y2,Y1,Y0:    first divisor's numerators, u then v, DESCENDING,
//                               over Z1 at the declared weights
//        Xp2,Xp1,Xp0, Yp2,Yp1,Yp0: second divisor's, over Z2, DESCENDING
//        f5:                    curve coefficient, RAW
//
// Output: upp3, upp2, upp1, upp0, vpp2, vpp1, vpp0, Znew -- 2g+2 values, the shipped
//         shape plus the denominator. upp3 is the literal 1: u is monic and
//         wt(u_3) = 0.
//
// Description: Adds two degree-3 divisors whose supports are disjoint, both in
//              projective coordinates with unrelated denominators. Measured
//              86M 13S 61A 1C 0I. Roughly 13M of that is unifying the two
//              denominators -- Z := Z1*Z2 and the lifts -- which is the price of the
//              general case and is exactly what Deg3ADDmix avoids.
//
//              Mapping VERIFIED against reference.add, not inferred: X/Y is the
//              first operand over Z1 and Xp/Yp the second over Z2. The transposed
//              assignment disagrees.
///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
Deg3ADD:= function(Z1, Z2, X2, X1, X0, Y2, Y1, Y0, Xp2, Xp1, Xp0, Yp2, Yp1, Yp0, f5)
    Z := Z1*Z2;
    a2 := Z2^2;
    a3 := a2*Z2;
    a4 := a2^2;
    a5 := a4*Z2;
    a6 := a3^2;
    a7 := a6*Z2;
    b2 := Z1^2;
    b3 := b2*Z1;
    b4 := b2^2;
    b5 := b4*Z1;
    b6 := b3^2;
    b7 := b6*Z1;
    u2 := X2*a2;
    u1 := X1*a4;
    u0 := X0*a6;
    v2 := Y2*a3;
    v1 := Y1*a5;
    v0 := Y0*a7;
    up2 := Xp2*b2;
    up1 := Xp1*b4;
    up0 := Xp0*b6;
    vp2 := Yp2*b3;
    vp1 := Yp1*b5;
    vp0 := Yp0*b7;
    Z4 := a4*b4;
    F5 := f5*Z4;
    t1 := u0 - up0;
    t4 := u1 - up1;
    t7 := u2 - up2;
    t2 := -up0*t7;
    t5 := t1 - up1*t7;
    t8 := t4 - up2*t7;
    m7 := t4*t8 - t5*t7;
    m8 := t2*t7 - t1*t8;
    m9 := t1*t5 - t2*t4;
    m5 := m9 + up2*m8;
    m2 := -up0*m7;
    m1 := m5 + up1*m7;
    d := t1*m1 + t4*m2 + t2*m8;
    k2 := F5 - u1 + u2^2;
    vt2 := vp2 - v2;
    vt1 := vp1 - v1;
    vt0 := vp0 - v0;
    m3 := -up0*m8;
    sp0 := vt0*m1 + vt1*m2 + vt2*m3;
    sp1 := vt0*(m8 + up2*m7) + vt1*m5 + vt2*(m2 - up1*m8);
    sp2 := vt0*m7 + vt1*m8 + vt2*m9;
    A2 := sp2^2;
    G := up2*sp2 - sp1;
    R1 := up1*A2 - sp1*G - sp0*sp2;
    R0 := up0*A2 - sp0*G;
    P := sp2*d;
    P2 := P^2;
    P3 := P2*P;
    P4 := P2^2;
    P5 := P4*P;
    P6 := P3^2;
    P7 := P6*P;
    W := P*d;
    Ls1 := sp1*W;
    Lw3 := W^2;
    Lr1 := R1;
    Lr0 := R0*P2;
    Lu2 := u2*P2;
    Lup2 := up2*P2;
    Lv2 := v2*P3;
    Lvt2 := vt2*P3;
    Lkmu := (k2 - up1)*P4;
    Lu1 := u1*P4;
    Lv1 := v1*P5;
    Lu0 := u0*P6;
    Lv0 := v0*P7;
    Lt7 := Lu2 - Lup2;
    Lv2p := Lv2 + Lv2 + Lvt2;
    Lq0 := Lup2 - Ls1;
    LM10 := Lvt2 + Lr0 + Lr1*Lt7;
    LM21 := -Lu2 - Ls1;
    LM20 := Lkmu + Ls1*(Lu2 + Lup2) + Lr1*Lv2p;
    LE := LM21 - Lr1^2;
    Lupp2 := LE + Lq0;
    Lupp1 := LM20 - Lr1*(LM10 + Lr0) + LM21*Lq0;
    Lupp0 := LM20*Lq0 - Lr0*LM10;
    Lt1 := Lr0 - Lr1*Lq0;
    Lt2 := (Lu2 - Lq0)*Lt1 + LE*Lw3;
    Lvpp2 := Lr1*(Lu2 - Lupp2) + Lt1 + Lw3 - Lv2;
    Lvpp1 := Lr1*(Lu1 - Lupp1) + Lt2 - Lv1;
    Lvpp0 := Lr1*(Lu0 - Lupp0) + Lu1*Lt1 - Lq0*Lt2 + Lupp1*Lw3 - Lv0;
    Znew := P*Z;
    return 1, Lupp2, Lupp1, Lupp0, Lvpp2, Lvpp1, Lvpp0, Znew;
end function;

///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// ADD():
// Input: u, v, Z:     polynomial Mumford coordinates and denominator of D1
//        up, vp, Zp:  the same for D2. Zp = 1 selects the mixed path.
//        f:           curve polynomial
//
// Output: projective upp3..upp0, vpp2..vpp0, Znew for D1 + D2
//
// Description: Dispatches on degree and on whether the second operand is affine,
//              and REFUSES everything else. Returns Znew = 0 on refusal -- NOT the
//              affine files' all-(-1) convention, because -1 is nonzero and a
//              normalising caller would build a garbage divisor from it and count it
//              as a disagreement rather than a skip. Zero is the one value every
//              consumer here already refuses.
//
//              Degree tests only: no Resultant, which maginterp does not implement.
//              The frequent-path condition needs no test anyway -- Znew = d*sp2*Z
//              vanishes exactly when the input leaves it.
///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
ADD:= function(u, v, Z, up, vp, Zp, f)//startIGNORE
    // Extracted and NOT USED, and not deletable: driver.read_support infers the
    // family's domain by contrast, so an absent extraction reads as "assumed zero".
    // PR21's f7 := Coeff(f, 7) is the precedent.
    f2 := Coeff(f,2);
    f1 := Coeff(f,1);
    f0 := Coeff(f,0);
    if Degree(u) eq 3 and Degree(up) eq 3 then
        if IsOne(Zp) then
            return Deg3ADDmix(Z, Coeff(f,5),
                              Coeff(up,2), Coeff(up,1), Coeff(up,0),
                              Coeff(vp,2), Coeff(vp,1), Coeff(vp,0),
                              Coeff(u,0), Coeff(u,1), Coeff(u,2),
                              Coeff(v,2), Coeff(v,1), Coeff(v,0));
        end if;
        return Deg3ADD(Z, Zp,
                       Coeff(u,2), Coeff(u,1), Coeff(u,0),
                       Coeff(v,2), Coeff(v,1), Coeff(v,0),
                       Coeff(up,2), Coeff(up,1), Coeff(up,0),
                       Coeff(vp,2), Coeff(vp,1), Coeff(vp,0), Coeff(f,5));
    end if;
    "PROJECTIVE ADD: only deg u = deg up = 3 is explicit in this file";
    return 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0;
end function;//endIGNORE
